# Drop an object from the world (perception no longer sees it).
# Refused (success=false) for an unknown object_id: the scene is left untouched.
string object_id
---
# success=true means the write committed atomically to disk; error is empty.
# success=false means the write did NOT durably commit. Two cases, told apart
# by error: the store refused the input and left the scene unchanged, or the
# atomic disk write failed and the change is held in the store's memory to be
# re-written on the next mutation (robot_world's dirty-flag design, D23) --
# not "rejected".
bool success
string error
